 "history": "With the philabeg and the plaid Highlanders wore short hose of tartan or diced cloth cut on the bias and sewn, reaching to below the knee and gartered there, the top turned down (the NMS kilt suit's hose; Burt describes the dress in the 1720s-30s) [EU-H2][EU-H5b]. Highland dress was banned in Scotland 'for man or boy' from 1747 to 1782 (soldiers exempt; the Act did not run in America) [EU-H1].",
